{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 56, :comments ["<b>For the swelling, and for the scurf, and for the bright spot.</b> Even though they resemble one another in that each of them is white, and their rulings are the same and they combine according to what is received in tradition, nevertheless, one who comes to rule on afflictions must be expert in the gradations of whiteness and their locations — for the site of a boil or burn is judged by mixed appearances and yellowing, while the site of hair is not judged by appearance at all."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:16.991958552Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}